{
  "module": "modulo02-integracao-apis-llms/01-smart-model-router-gateway",
  "concepts": ["model-routing", "rest-api"],
  "recorded": "Every case passed against the original with Node.js 26.12.1, @openrouter/sdk 0.5.1, and fastify 5.7.4, run as \"node {program}.ts\", where the programs are the gateway, src/index, and the module's end-to-end tests, tests/router.e2e.test. The original always listens on port 3000 and always calls OpenRouter's address, so the copy that produced these cases listens on PORT and prints it, falling back to 3000, a two-line change in src/index.ts, and passes OPENAI_BASE_URL to the OpenRouter client as its server URL, a one-line change in src/openrouterService.ts. No OpenRouter key was available, so the answers were recorded from Ollama 0.40.11 with llama2-uncensored:7b standing in for the routed models and wrapped in OpenRouter's documented response format, the one exemplo-11-openrouter keeps, and the model in each answer is the one the module's tests expect OpenRouter to pick for that sorting, which is synthesized. The tests program is checked by its requests, in the order the original runs its tests, and by whether it succeeds or fails, never by its report, because every test runner prints its own and some fail with their own exit code. Fastify's error bodies are checked by status code, statusCode, and error, with any non-empty message, because the validation messages come from Ajv, except the unknown route, whose message is short and checked exactly. A provider failure is never checked, because the original sets status 500 without sending it, so the request never gets an answer.",
  "prepare": {
    "setup": ["npm ci --no-audit --no-fund"],
    "patches": [
      {
        "file": "src/index.ts",
        "find": "{ port: 3000, host",
        "replace": "{ port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? 3000), host"
      },
      {
        "file": "src/index.ts",
        "find": "'server running at 3000'",
        "replace": "`server running at ${process.env.PORT ?? 3000}`"
      },
      {
        "file": "src/openrouterService.ts",
        "find": "xTitle: config.xTitle\n",
        "replace": "xTitle: config.xTitle,\n            serverURL: process.env.OPENAI_BASE_URL\n"
      }
    ]
  },
  "originals": ["node {program}.ts"],
  "env": {
    "OPENROUTER_API_KEY": "replay"
  },
